{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787178589141140001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"steep-tired-whimbrel","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b5eddb4d5fa90a89c1609bb3300f8699e8e3d8b83ecd1f7dc2f5c776634f6e70","event_uuid":"b85e143d-55d1-40ff-8c76-f1681a5e7f59","position":{"commit_sha":"b8a75f15d85badbd419bc96d0bc70ae5b776f7c6","position":"1787175607648248001-b85e143d-55d1-40ff-8c76-f1681a5e7f59"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a0dc8fae9427eeb32cba8254a776f7669434e50befe1300bb0464d1c453948cb","event_uuid":"094991a3-bd82-415a-ac3a-e36f87b0cd74","position":{"commit_sha":"5869523410b4caa9eed747ebd8946cb04075e00a","position":"1787175638163802001-094991a3-bd82-415a-ac3a-e36f87b0cd74"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787175607648248001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"094991a3-bd82-415a-ac3a-e36f87b0cd74","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"23b2-1a94-6a01-466b"}],"description":"## Problem\n`gate_enabled` (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:79-87) returns a BARE BOOL that is `False` for TWO\nmaterially different states:\n\n  * the gate is genuinely turned off (a deliberate policy choice), and\n  * the gate's configuration could not be READ (a fault).\n\nWorse, the unreadable case **fails OPEN**. An unreadable or malformed config therefore silently\nDISABLES the completion-verification gate, and every downstream reader — including\n`_completion_precheck` — sees a state indistinguishable from an operator having turned the gate off\non purpose. A fault is laundered into a policy choice, and the gate stops protecting anything\nwithout anyone being told.\n\nThis is a latent defect with standalone value: it is worth fixing whether or not any dependent work\nis ever built.\n\n## Approach\nReturn a TRI-STATE (gate on / gate off / gate config unreadable) instead of a bool, and fail CLOSED\non unreadable rather than open. Fix it at the SOURCE in `gate_enabled` rather than recomputing the\ndistinction at each call site — a second config read in a second place is a copy that will drift out\nof sync with the first.\n\nUpdate all callers to handle the third state explicitly rather than defaulting it into either\nexisting branch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `gate_enabled` returns a three-valued result distinguishing enabled / disabled /\n      config-unreadable; no caller can conflate the latter two.\n- [ ] An unreadable or malformed gate config FAILS CLOSED (the gate is treated as active), and the\n      condition is surfaced rather than swallowed.\n- [ ] A held-out test seeds an unreadable config and asserts the gate does NOT silently disable —\n      demonstrated RED before the fix, not merely green after.\n- [ ] Every existing `gate_enabled` caller is updated to handle the third state explicitly; a grep\n      for call sites shows none relying on bool truthiness.\n- [ ] Existing gate on/off behaviour is unchanged for readable configs (existing tests pass unmodified).\n\n## Provenance\nSplit out per operator decision 2026-08-19 from `mechanical-coherent-wolverine` (23b2-1a94), where\nthis surfaced as plan-review R3's first blocking finding: 'gate_enabled must distinguish gate-off\nfrom config-unreadable, or the expectation must be computed somewhere that can see the difference.\nIts current fail-open bool is the blocker.' It is filed separately because the defect stands on its\nown, and because wolverine cannot author its `gate_unreadable` acceptance criteria until this\ntri-state's shape is settled.\n\nCoordinate with RP-06 (`uneducated-habitual-primate`, 'Unified effective-policy discovery for review\ngates'): RP-06's effective-policy snapshot should CONSUME this tri-state, not produce its own. This\nwas deliberately NOT folded into RP-06 so that a small, independently-landable fix is not coupled to\na large program's schedule.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f5c4-b2d1-4503-4bfe","ticket_type":"bug","title":"gate_enabled fails OPEN and collapses gate-off with config-unreadable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b85e143d-55d1-40ff-8c76-f1681a5e7f59","094991a3-bd82-415a-ac3a-e36f87b0cd74"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787178589141140001,"uuid":"967c99b0-d4e5-4495-af75-60f0a8dd876f"}